<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The adaptive launcher icon.

  From API 26 up, `@mipmap/ic_launcher` resolves to this file rather than to the PNGs in the
  `mipmap-<density>` folders, and the launcher composites the two layers and then crops the result to
  whatever mask it has chosen - a circle, a squircle, a rounded square, or on some OEM skins a shape
  nobody else uses. That is why the layers are 108 dp when the icon is 48: the outer 18 dp on each
  side is margin the system is allowed to throw away, and only the middle 66 dp is guaranteed to
  survive. `crates/playback/km-display/examples/icon.rs` sizes the microphone to fit inside that circle.

  Both layers are generated. The background is not a flat color because the icon's ground is a
  radial wash, and a `<color>` element cannot hold one; the PNG carries the same wash the foreground
  was drawn against, so the two line up into a single image whatever the mask does to the edges.

  The PNGs in `mipmap-<density>` are unreachable at our minSdk of 26 - nothing that can install the
  app is old enough to read them. They are kept because they are 68 KB in total and they are what the
  platform falls back to if this file is ever wrong or the minimum ever drops, which is a cheaper
  insurance premium than the failure it covers.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_background" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground" />
</adaptive-icon>
